{"items":[{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"3bb6fd009e0b30629a357b94088580cdc7e8cc44df0de279cda23687f3a8874d","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/block-sparse-gpu-kernels","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"f0d270fbca2eedeae418","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/block-sparse-gpu-kernels","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-12-06T08:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We’re releasing highly-optimized GPU kernels for an underexplored class of neural network architectures: networks with block-sparse weights. Depending on the chosen sparsity, these kernels can run orders of magnitude faster than cuBLAS or cuSPARSE. We’ve used them to attain state-of-the-art results in text sentiment analysis and generative modeling of text and images.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Block-sparse GPU kernels","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/block-sparse-gpu-kernels"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"cf5c09e9c932a493180c1b0dc0e551ead6a572e0b0867a96aabed6276d2f962b","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/learning-sparse-neural-networks-through-l0-regularization","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"6427559453119304b5e3","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/learning-sparse-neural-networks-through-l0-regularization","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-12-04T08:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Learning sparse neural networks through L₀ regularization","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/learning-sparse-neural-networks-through-l0-regularization"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"1294acea2f041941a4f9496c99d1419d4d3adabc0ecb608d44bb135151d883ba","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/interpretable-and-pedagogical-examples","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"be84f3d01add7fe83fa8","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/interpretable-and-pedagogical-examples","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-11-02T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Interpretable and pedagogical examples","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/interpretable-and-pedagogical-examples"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"a4dd8f51d69505c8b6ffccd9bc624e2d54670cf329358ebeeb71ec6432e621fe","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/learning-a-hierarchy","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"3c2715ba8c646fe77a57","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/learning-a-hierarchy","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-10-26T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We’ve developed a hierarchical reinforcement learning algorithm that learns high-level actions useful for solving a range of tasks, allowing fast solving of tasks requiring thousands of timesteps. Our algorithm, when applied to a set of navigation problems, discovers a set of high-level actions for walking and crawling in different directions, which enables the agent to master new navigation tasks quickly.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Learning a hierarchy","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/learning-a-hierarchy"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"1b724dff9022547c4ca463982d7c236d380959a4f10d4cf1dcbef4b14b1ac7f5","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/generalizing-from-simulation","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"2d6c85bd3e8673cf6c78","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/generalizing-from-simulation","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-10-19T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"Our latest robotics techniques allow robot controllers, trained entirely in simulation and deployed on physical robots, to react to unplanned changes in the environment as they solve simple tasks. That is, we’ve used these techniques to build closed-loop systems rather than open-loop ones as before.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Generalizing from simulation","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/generalizing-from-simulation"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"7a7e103b6eace75b0f3d1796ad55a74d1c9a8521da727a578d5b7e57ea156c6c","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/sim-to-real-transfer-of-robotic-control-with-dynamics-randomization","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"cafc87444fd3659fca60","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/sim-to-real-transfer-of-robotic-control-with-dynamics-randomization","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-10-18T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Sim-to-real transfer of robotic control with dynamics randomization","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/sim-to-real-transfer-of-robotic-control-with-dynamics-randomization"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"d18c788a08bb29828384f1af9e4d887955fa6b554d4d7d3e871abdf96e6deaa6","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/asymmetric-actor-critic-for-image-based-robot-learning","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"81a665efcb32ae13d41e","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/asymmetric-actor-critic-for-image-based-robot-learning","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-10-18T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Asymmetric actor critic for image-based robot learning","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/asymmetric-actor-critic-for-image-based-robot-learning"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"c461476f19c6a0708fb876be6b5b1846b2617d834d07fb5b6969470604f60440","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/domain-randomization-and-generative-models-for-robotic-grasping","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"740d039f34215d949d80","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/domain-randomization-and-generative-models-for-robotic-grasping","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-10-17T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Domain randomization and generative models for robotic grasping","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/domain-randomization-and-generative-models-for-robotic-grasping"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"37cf08e2b3d0cc77436397191250634ab02a9073386d942eb0982da3f22d74ac","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/meta-learning-for-wrestling","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"6b89bea3012e9afe8184","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/meta-learning-for-wrestling","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-10-11T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We show that for the task of simulated robot wrestling, a meta-learning agent can learn to quickly defeat a stronger non-meta-learning agent, and also show that the meta-learning agent can adapt to physical malfunction.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Meta-learning for wrestling","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/meta-learning-for-wrestling"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"805a7d83508b730b3d239eac56b15977c04c5ca84ca2674a4bb4bb3310dbf29f","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/competitive-self-play","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"581dd87d0e73fa146e82","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/competitive-self-play","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-10-11T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We’ve found that self-play allows simulated AIs to discover physical skills like tackling, ducking, faking, kicking, catching, and diving for the ball, without explicitly designing an environment with these skills in mind. Self-play ensures that the environment is always the right difficulty for an AI to improve. Taken alongside our Dota 2 self-play results, we have increasing confidence that self-play will be a core part of powerful AI systems in the future.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Competitive self-play","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/competitive-self-play"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"a769a73993d8d7d28ff3dac07379d269eaebe354c77911f89dd285fa9e5601e2","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/nonlinear-computation-in-deep-linear-networks","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"994b9539f35515e9c341","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/nonlinear-computation-in-deep-linear-networks","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-09-29T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Nonlinear computation in deep linear networks","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/nonlinear-computation-in-deep-linear-networks"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"9c0ce6a4df88aff0190426fd82eca25122aefb715679db67139adaeefc268076","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/learning-to-model-other-minds","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"22f524cf064dacee6ccf","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/learning-to-model-other-minds","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-09-14T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We’re releasing an algorithm which accounts for the fact that other agents are learning too, and discovers self-interested yet collaborative strategies like tit-for-tat in the iterated prisoner’s dilemma. This algorithm, Learning with Opponent-Learning Awareness (LOLA), is a small step towards agents that model other minds.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Learning to model other minds","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/learning-to-model-other-minds"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"06f7dbcdf2de1a0bdfe1ec6bc59ad2a10b77192c2881b4c9fdd894d3320b96ab","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/learning-with-opponent-learning-awareness","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"df4bf285848c6cddc998","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/learning-with-opponent-learning-awareness","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-09-13T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Learning with opponent-learning awareness","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/learning-with-opponent-learning-awareness"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"b9480fa73babdf0a8dd57d4a363e4da17de23b197f6146ec19781699f4045878","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/openai-baselines-acktr-a2c","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"7d4417b6f1fa840b3406","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/openai-baselines-acktr-a2c","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-08-18T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We’re releasing two new OpenAI Baselines implementations: ACKTR and A2C. A2C is a synchronous, deterministic variant of Asynchronous Advantage Actor Critic (A3C) which we’ve found gives equal performance. ACKTR is a more sample-efficient reinforcement learning algorithm than TRPO and A2C, and requires only slightly more computation than A2C per update.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"OpenAI Baselines: ACKTR & A2C","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/openai-baselines-acktr-a2c"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"888d0bda48f65b4f91c307a5a02e968bacdf9a28524c23457379d6251ea876e9","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/more-on-dota-2","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"7e4bda609cfe4368df86","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/more-on-dota-2","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-08-16T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"Our Dota 2 result shows that self-play can catapult the performance of machine learning systems from far below human level to superhuman, given sufficient compute. In the span of a month, our system went from barely matching a high-ranked player to beating the top pros and has continued to improve since then. Supervised deep learning systems can only be as good as their training datasets, but in self-play systems, the available data improves automatically as the agent gets better.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"More on Dota 2","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/more-on-dota-2"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"249a7be28cc36e4b63d5f53da8e21ec117b93bba7eb996716da4a7fc718d0ec3","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/dota-2","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"e636241aa38390682555","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/dota-2","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-08-11T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We’ve created a bot which beats the world’s top professionals at 1v1 matches of Dota 2 under standard tournament rules. The bot learned the game from scratch by self-play, and does not use imitation learning or tree search. This is a step towards building AI systems which accomplish well-defined goals in messy, complicated situations involving real humans.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Dota 2","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/dota-2"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"323d67a1cfbc1ea0158f177306c618f1227b6c21316466f3d9deec954eceaa4c","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/gathering-human-feedback","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"698b1890fdd155cb5e24","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/gathering-human-feedback","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-08-03T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"RL-Teacher is an open-source implementation of our interface to train AIs via occasional human feedback rather than hand-crafted reward functions. The underlying technique was developed as a step towards safe AI systems, but also applies to reinforcement learning problems with rewards that are hard to specify.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Gathering human feedback","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/gathering-human-feedback"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"e574d2b4331a604bf4dcdb00d9bb0b1fcf39a0b6e28fbd4cf99a0eec979be690","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/better-exploration-with-parameter-noise","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"96322b294d065cf6a4d9","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/better-exploration-with-parameter-noise","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-07-27T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We’ve found that adding adaptive noise to the parameters of reinforcement learning algorithms frequently boosts performance. This exploration method is simple to implement and very rarely decreases performance, so it’s worth trying on any problem.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Better exploration with parameter noise","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/better-exploration-with-parameter-noise"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"604c3ba3f192882caaaeeb778726bf98df67ae3000ccf5866d2e2ba67f3afabe","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/openai-baselines-ppo","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"9ab874ca894491c8d411","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/openai-baselines-ppo","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-07-20T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We’re releasing a new class of reinforcement learning algorithms, Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO), which perform comparably or better than state-of-the-art approaches while being much simpler to implement and tune. PPO has become the default reinforcement learning algorithm at OpenAI because of its ease of use and good performance.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Proximal Policy Optimization","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/openai-baselines-ppo"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"9ef58c41a4b391c80765bfd4a50074975f2edf9893aef48ea61dfcbf1ebcb77b","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/robust-adversarial-inputs","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"0ea53cd481f01fe279b8","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/robust-adversarial-inputs","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2017-07-17T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":1,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We’ve created images that reliably fool neural network classifiers when viewed from varied scales and perspectives. This challenges a claim from last week that self-driving cars would be hard to trick maliciously since they capture images from multiple scales, angles, perspectives, and the like.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Robust adversarial inputs","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/robust-adversarial-inputs"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"7661bbd825a506e1fa0124f351b3d3eaceb0b2ce5f690b5e5640ce1e1afba11c","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/hindsight-experience-replay","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"c1af6b88bb0c5265898e","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/hindsight-exp